s8-5-p31 : Block
s8-5-p31 = prose (cons "An allocation operation consumes a state and returns either an allocation failure or a pointer and an updated state satisfying the allocation conditions. A region allocator can maintain an interval `[base,end)` and a cursor. Allocation of `n` aligned bytes computes the aligned cursor and advances it only after checking that the calculation and resulting range are valid. Deallocation ends the applicable lifetime. The logical state can contain metadata erased from the native representation after its uses have been discharged." nil)
